# Security

- Never expose database credentials, SMTP credentials, auth secrets or private environment variables.
- Never trust client-side validation alone.
- Validate and sanitize server-side input.
- Enforce authorization server-side; hiding UI controls is not authorization.
- Use secure password hashing.
- Protect admin routes and server operations.
- Consider SQL injection, XSS, CSRF where applicable, abuse/rate limiting and file upload risks.
- Validate uploaded file type and size.
- Do not log passwords, tokens or sensitive user data.
- Use environment variables for secrets and deployment-specific configuration.
- Never weaken security just to make a feature work.
